ha-dobiss-nxt
=============

This project is a rewrite of prior work and would not exist without it.

Original work
-------------
  "dobiss" custom integration for Home Assistant
  "pydobiss" Python library
  Copyright (c) 2020-2025 Kester Aernoudt
  https://github.com/kesteraernoudt/dobiss
  https://pypi.org/project/pydobiss/
  Licensed under the MIT License.

Kester Aernoudt reverse-engineered and documented the Dobiss NXT behaviour that
this integration relies on, wrote the first working Home Assistant integration
for it, and maintained it from 2020 through 2025. The device model, the way
up/down relay pairs are matched into covers, and the overall shape of the
platform layout all originate with him.

This project
------------
  Copyright (c) 2026 Matthias Van der Elst
  https://github.com/MatthiasVanDE/ha-dobiss-nxt
  Licensed under the MIT License.

What changed relative to the original:
  - the pydobiss dependency was replaced by a typed async client inside this
    integration, so there is no longer an unmaintained pinned dependency;
  - the xknx==0.9.4 pin was dropped in favour of an internal travel calculator;
  - entities report availability from the live connection state;
  - the Dobiss NXT energy meter (address 209) is exposed as sensors;
  - several defects in the original were fixed. They are listed in CHANGELOG.md
    and were reported upstream.

